34,2,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
35,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"It appears our financial situation is more constrained than I had hoped. The development allocation is significantly lower this year, and we must be mindful of how we utilize our physical space to ensure funding.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, constraints are merely boundaries to work within. My findings show that previous trials, like the call-back system, actually worked—until they were abandoned. It seems we have a habit of ignoring success.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Midori,,"That is a concerning point, Shion. Looking at the staffing, I've found that ward nursing vacancies are rising and agency costs are increasing, though midwifery actually has some unusual slack. We must be careful not to overburden our teams.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"Wow, we're really tight on space! The parking fills up by eleven and the shuttle only hits a few villages. Plus, the booking system misses a lot of work. I'm worried we'll just jam everything up!","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems we have much to consider. I found that some of our past joint efforts struggled when responsibilities weren't clear, and agreements with outside partners can take a very long time to finalize. We must be gentle with our planning.","{""words"":41,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, your point about clarity is vital. Given the reduced budget and the fact that off-site contacts bring no revenue, we must prioritize programs that are financially sustainable and utilize our on-site facilities efficiently.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, focusing solely on on-site efficiency is a narrow view. If we ignore proven successes like the call-back trial just because they aren't ""on-site,"" we are simply repeating the mistake of burying effective care.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, I understand your point, but we must consider the people. If we implement a program without enough staff, the burden falls on those already struggling. We need a solution that fits our current capacity.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, I totally agree! If the parking is already full and the booking system is missing stuff, adding more people might just make everything crash. We need something that fits without making a huge mess!","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"It is so heartening to see you all caring so deeply for the staff and the patients. Perhaps we should look for a path that is simple and kind to everyone, avoiding any overly complex arrangements.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shion, I do not wish to bury success, but we cannot ignore the ledger. If we choose a program that generates no tariff and drains a shrinking budget, it will fail within a year regardless of its clinical merit.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, your obsession with the ledger is predictable, but short-sighted. A program that fails due to lack of funding is a tragedy; a program that fails because we are too timid to implement proven results is a farce.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, @Shion, please, let's try to find a middle ground. We can't ignore the budget, but we also can't ignore the staff. If we pick a program that's too demanding, our nurses will burn out.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Jonathan, @Shion, please don't fight! We just need to make sure the hospital doesn't seize up. If we pick something that needs more rooms or parking, it won't matter how much money we have!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"Now, now, let us all take a deep breath. We are all speaking from a place of care for our hospital. Perhaps the most sustainable choice is one that requires very little from our tired staff and our limited space.","{""words"":40,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I agree with Shizue. We must seek a balance. A program that is modest in its spatial requirements, gentle on our staff, and generates a steady on-site tariff is the only way to ensure long-term survival.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
51,2,4,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, your ""balance"" sounds like a recipe for mediocrity. If we only choose what is easy and profitable, we aren't providing care; we're running a business. I'll support a choice that actually delivers results.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
52,2,4,talk,Midori,,I hope we can find a way to deliver those results without sacrificing our team's well-being. Let's look at the candidates and see if any of them truly balance effectiveness with our current staffing reality.,"{""words"":35,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
53,2,4,talk,Kenji,,I'm with Midori! Let's just hope the candidates don't need a million new parking spots or a whole new booking system. I'm ready to see the list and find something that actually fits!,"{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
54,2,4,talk,Shizue,,"I agree with you all. Let us look upon the candidates with open hearts and minds, keeping in mind that a gentle start is often the most lasting one. I am ready.","{""words"":32,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
55,3,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
56,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
