59,3,,status,Midori,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
60,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Looking at the options, Candidate B, the Day Rehabilitation Unit, seems most viable. It utilizes on-site space to generate tariffs and provides a structured environment that avoids the funding pitfalls of off-site care.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,1,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, your preference for B is as predictable as it is dull. Candidate A, the Home Follow-Up Team, mirrors the call-back trial's success. Why gamble on a new unit when we have proven results?","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,1,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, I worry that Candidate A would put too much pressure on our ward nurses, who are already struggling with vacancies. Candidate C, the Perinatal Support Service, seems much more sustainable given the slack in midwifery.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Jonathan, B sounds like it would need way more rooms and parking, and we're already full! @Midori, C sounds better, but @Shion, D might be cool because it coordinates things without needing more space!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[""Jonathan"",""Midori"",""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, your thought for the midwives is very sweet. However, I worry that Candidate C, being a joint effort, might struggle if the departments cannot agree on the burden. Perhaps Candidate D is a gentler path for us all.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, @Kenji, Candidate D is an attractive compromise, but we must consider the funding. If coordination happens off-site, we lose the tariff. Candidate B is the only one ensuring a steady revenue stream to cover running costs.","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,2,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, your obsession with revenue is blinding you. Candidate D is a logical evolution of care, but Candidate A is a proven victory. Why are we so afraid to actually help patients just because it's not ""profitable""?","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,2,talk,Midori,,"@Jonathan, we can't prioritize revenue over our people. Candidate B requires physical therapists, but we've lost so many to the city. Candidate C uses existing capacity without adding stress to the exhausted ward staff. It's the most balanced choice.","{""words"":39,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, I like C, but will it fill up the parking lot even more? @Jonathan, B is definitely too big for our space! I think D is the safest because it's about organizing, not adding more crowds!","{""words"":37,""mentions"":[""Midori"",""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Jonathan, I understand your worries about the budget, but a program that fails because it is too complex is a greater waste. Candidate D seems to avoid the pitfalls of joint rotas and long agreements.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,"@Shizue, @Kenji, if we choose Candidate D, we must ensure the coordination is based on-site to secure the tariff. Otherwise, we are simply planning for a future deficit. Between D and B, D is certainly more spatialy modest.","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Shizue"",""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,3,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, you're still trying to fit a square peg into a round hole. Candidate A is the only one with a track record of success here. Why settle for ""modest"" when we can have ""proven""?","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,3,talk,Midori,,"@Shion, ""proven"" doesn't help if the staff are too exhausted to implement it. Candidate A would likely fall on the ward nurses, and they are already at a breaking point. Candidate C is the only one that truly respects our current staffing balance.","{""words"":43,""mentions"":[""Shion""],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,3,talk,Kenji,,"@Midori, I see your point about the nurses! But if C brings in lots of new parents for classes, won't the parking lot just overflow? D seems like the best way to help without making a huge mess!","{""words"":38,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"@Midori, your kindness toward the nurses is truly touching. However, I fear Candidate C's joint nature might lead to the same disagreements we've seen before. Candidate D feels like a peaceful choice that helps everyone.","{""words"":35,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
75,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,"I see that a consensus is forming around Candidate D. While I still worry about the long-term funding, it is the most reasonable compromise regarding space and staffing. I will cast my vote for Candidate D.","{""words"":36,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
76,3,4,talk,Shion,,"@Jonathan, your ""reasonable compromise"" is just a surrender to the path of least resistance. I refuse to support a choice based on fear of the ledger. I vote for Candidate A.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Jonathan""],""raw_differs"":false}"
77,3,4,talk,Midori,,"I truly believe we must protect our staff from further burnout. Candidate A is too risky for our nurses, and B is impossible for our therapists. I vote for Candidate C.","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
78,3,4,talk,Kenji,,"I'm going with Candidate D! It helps the patients without needing more parking or rooms, and it won't make the booking system crash. It's the only one that actually fits! I vote for D!","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
79,3,4,talk,Shizue,,"It has been a most thoughtful discussion. While I admire the passion for each option, I believe Candidate D is the most sustainable and peaceful choice for our hospital. I vote for Candidate D.","{""words"":34,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
